WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.100
-Welcome to the show.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.400
It is so nice to see you.
It's so nice to meet you.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.701
-It's so nice to meet you.
Honestly, what a treat!

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:09.133
-Everyone around the office
loves you, and I go, "Yeah."

00:00:09.133 --> 00:00:11.434
But for all different reasons.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.868
They go,
"I know her from her stand-up.

00:00:13.868 --> 00:00:15.133
Her specials are unbelievable."

00:00:15.133 --> 00:00:16.601
I go, "Yeah,
that's how I know her."

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.767
They go, "Then also, she's on --

00:00:18.767 --> 00:00:20.467
Co-hosts 'Wipeout'
with John Cena."

00:00:20.467 --> 00:00:22.334
I go, "Oh, yeah, she does."
-Mm-hmm.

00:00:22.334 --> 00:00:24.400
-And then someone's like,
"No, no, her podcast is like

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:26.033
unbelievable."
Then someone goes,

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:27.701
"No, she's on
a different podcast."

00:00:27.701 --> 00:00:29.934
Then I go,
"She's on 'Grand Crew.'"

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:33.467
-Yeah, I'm tired.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:33.467 --> 00:00:35.334
Yes, I'm exhausted.
-I mean, wow!

00:00:35.334 --> 00:00:38.367
You are kicking butt right now!
-Yeah, it's really nice.

00:00:38.367 --> 00:00:41.234
I get recognized a lot by, like,
little kids for "Nailed It,"

00:00:41.234 --> 00:00:42.801
which is weird
because I talk about

00:00:42.801 --> 00:00:44.968
non-child stuff in my stand-up.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:44.968 --> 00:00:46.968
-Okay, yeah.
Can you tell what people

00:00:46.968 --> 00:00:48.434
know you from what show?
-Ooh, yeah.

00:00:48.434 --> 00:00:50.367
If it's a gay man,
it's "Why Won't You Date Me?"

00:00:50.367 --> 00:00:53.701
which is my podcast
about why I'm single.

00:00:53.701 --> 00:00:55.767
[ Laughter ]

00:00:55.767 --> 00:00:58.767
But people love yelling
"Nailed it" at me,

00:00:58.767 --> 00:01:00.200
and I was telling this
to John Cena, I was like,

00:01:00.200 --> 00:01:02.000
"Oh, my God, it's so awful.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:03.734
They're just screaming
'Nailed it' at me."

00:01:03.734 --> 00:01:06.801
And he said, "Nicole,
people are just trying

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.000
to identify with you,
come to you,

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.901
have a commonality with you."

00:01:11.901 --> 00:01:15.200
And I was like, "Huh. You are
a wise, wise wrestling man."

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:16.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:16.667 --> 00:01:18.734
-He is a very wise man.
-He is.

00:01:18.734 --> 00:01:20.801
-It's unbelievable.
-Oh, he's so sweet.

00:01:20.801 --> 00:01:24.033
-Is it true that people's kids
have gotten you jobs?

00:01:24.033 --> 00:01:25.434
-Okay.
They haven't gotten me jobs.

00:01:25.434 --> 00:01:27.200
They've gotten me auditions.
-Okay.

00:01:27.200 --> 00:01:29.267
-So, sometimes casting directors
will be like, "Oh, my God.

00:01:29.267 --> 00:01:31.234
My kid loves you so much
that we were like,

00:01:31.234 --> 00:01:33.901
'Let's bring you in
and not book you on it.'"

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:37.901
[ Laughter ]

00:01:37.901 --> 00:01:39.601
-"And I love driving
to Santa Monica

00:01:39.601 --> 00:01:42.000
in the middle of rush hour
to make you laugh!"

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:45.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:45.167 --> 00:01:47.634
-You host -- How many podcasts
do you host, four?

00:01:47.634 --> 00:01:49.501
-Four, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:01:49.501 --> 00:01:52.000
And right now, you're up for
Best Female Host

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.634
at the iHeartRadio
Podcast Awards.

00:01:53.634 --> 00:01:56.000
-Yes.
-Last year -- congratulations.

00:01:56.000 --> 00:01:57.267
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Thank you.

00:01:57.267 --> 00:02:01.167
-Last year, you beat out --
you beat Michelle Obama.

00:02:01.167 --> 00:02:03.133
-I know.
Isn't that wild?

00:02:03.133 --> 00:02:04.434
-I love it.
How exciting is that?

00:02:04.434 --> 00:02:05.634
-I know.
I think it's just people

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:09.067
identifying with
a desperate woman, you know?

00:02:09.067 --> 00:02:10.767
"I'm just looking
for the [bleep]"

00:02:10.767 --> 00:02:11.834
[ Laughter ]

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.067
"I just want it!"

00:02:14.067 --> 00:02:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:02:15.567 --> 00:02:16.767
"Where is it?"

00:02:16.767 --> 00:02:20.033
[ Laughter continues ]

00:02:20.033 --> 00:02:22.634
It's not back there."
-It's not there, no.

00:02:22.634 --> 00:02:26.834
But I --
[ Laughter ]

00:02:26.834 --> 00:02:30.267
Let's talk about
one of the other podcasts,

00:02:30.267 --> 00:02:32.300
which is called "Newcomers."
-Yes.

00:02:32.300 --> 00:02:34.901
-"Newcomers" -- genius idea.
You talk about things

00:02:34.901 --> 00:02:36.868
that everyone seems to know
about, except for you.

00:02:36.868 --> 00:02:38.334
-Yeah.
So it's me and Lauren Lapkus.

00:02:38.334 --> 00:02:40.000
She's so funny.
-She is so great!

00:02:40.000 --> 00:02:42.100
-I love her so much but we --
-"The Wrong Missy," by the way.

00:02:42.100 --> 00:02:43.767
-Yeah, it's so funny.
She falls off a cliff

00:02:43.767 --> 00:02:45.400
in one scene. I was like,
"Oh, my God, I'm dying."

00:02:45.400 --> 00:02:47.334
-She's brilliant in it.
Anyway...

00:02:47.334 --> 00:02:49.000
-But we watched

00:02:49.000 --> 00:02:51.601
"Lord of the Rings,"
and people like it.

00:02:51.601 --> 00:02:52.934
[ Laughter ]
-Wait.

00:02:52.934 --> 00:02:56.868
It's a very popular film.
[ Laughs ]

00:02:56.868 --> 00:02:58.534
A lot of people like it.
They love it.

00:02:58.534 --> 00:03:00.934
-But why --
It's just a magical hike.

00:03:00.934 --> 00:03:03.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.234 --> 00:03:06.868
They're going for this ring,
and then there's Gollum.

00:03:06.868 --> 00:03:08.901
He's got thinning hair,
and he's like, "My ring!"

00:03:08.901 --> 00:03:10.801
I'm like,
"You're just a woman, like,

00:03:10.801 --> 00:03:12.067
wanting a man
to propose to you."

00:03:12.067 --> 00:03:13.300
-Yeah, that's really, that's --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.701
-He's like, "Where's my ring?!"
Like, I'm Gollum.

00:03:15.701 --> 00:03:17.400
Oh, my God!
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.400 --> 00:03:18.901
-No, you're not Gollum!
-I'm Gollum!

00:03:18.901 --> 00:03:21.267
-You are not Gollum!
No, no, no.

00:03:21.267 --> 00:03:23.901
What other big franchises
is everyone into

00:03:23.901 --> 00:03:26.400
that you are not sure about?
-Oh, so, like, Marvel.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.367
I'm not a Marvel head.

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:29.701
-Have you seen any of them?

00:03:29.701 --> 00:03:32.100
-Well, I've seen "Black Panther"
'cause I'm Black, and --

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.934
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:03:36.934 --> 00:03:39.467
-Uh-huh, yep.
-We had to.

00:03:39.467 --> 00:03:40.901
-You had to.
-We had to!

00:03:40.901 --> 00:03:42.267
Otherwise, we'd lose our card.
-I understand.

00:03:42.267 --> 00:03:48.267
[ Laughter ]

00:03:48.267 --> 00:03:49.634
-Oh, there are my friends
over there. Hello.

00:03:49.634 --> 00:03:51.133
-Yeah.
-They know, they know.

00:03:51.133 --> 00:03:53.133
Y'all know, over there.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:53.133 --> 00:03:55.133
But I recently saw
the new "Spider-Man."

00:03:55.133 --> 00:03:58.100
I had not seen any of them.
I had so many questions.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:03:59.634
-Oh, yeah.
-And one of them --

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.767
I was like,
"Jamie Foxx is in 'Spider-Man'?"

00:04:01.767 --> 00:04:03.601
And then, my friend was like,
"Oh, yeah, this is a picture

00:04:03.601 --> 00:04:05.501
of him from the original one
that he was in."

00:04:05.501 --> 00:04:06.601
-Yeah.
-Yeah, and I was like --

00:04:06.601 --> 00:04:08.400
-We'll pull out this.
-What plot point

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.100
brought this man
to look like that?

00:04:10.100 --> 00:04:11.567
[ Laughter ]

00:04:11.567 --> 00:04:14.467
What -- What does Spider-Man
do to this --

00:04:14.467 --> 00:04:15.834
Is this --
What happened?

00:04:15.834 --> 00:04:18.400
Is it -- What?
How? Why?

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:20.267
I don't get it.
Someone did his hair and said,

00:04:20.267 --> 00:04:22.033
"Go to set."
Like what is that?

00:04:22.033 --> 00:04:23.367
[ Laughter ]

00:04:23.367 --> 00:04:24.734
-Yeah.
-I still haven't gotten

00:04:24.734 --> 00:04:26.701
any answers.
-Yeah, no --

00:04:26.701 --> 00:04:31.033
-It's wild to look at.
-But do you have any idea, like,

00:04:31.033 --> 00:04:34.033
maybe he might end up being a
villain or coming together to --

00:04:34.033 --> 00:04:35.834
-Well, I know he's a villain,
I think.

00:04:35.834 --> 00:04:37.534
-Okay.
-But he, like, didn't seem

00:04:37.534 --> 00:04:39.000
that mean, so I was like,
"Who's the real --"

00:04:39.000 --> 00:04:40.667
I don't -- There was
so many things going on.

00:04:40.667 --> 00:04:41.868
-Yeah.
-And then there was --

00:04:41.868 --> 00:04:43.100
Well, I don't want to ruin it.
Did everyone here

00:04:43.100 --> 00:04:45.968
see "Spider-Man"?
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:45.968 --> 00:04:48.601
-But just -- But don't --
You can't spoil anything.

00:04:48.601 --> 00:04:50.334
-Okay. Well, there was things
that happened that I was like,

00:04:50.334 --> 00:04:51.567
"What?"
-Be generic.

00:04:51.567 --> 00:04:53.901
-Be generic?

00:04:53.901 --> 00:04:57.267
I don't know what generic means.
[ Laughter ]

00:04:57.267 --> 00:04:58.567
I'm kidding.
-I know.

00:04:58.567 --> 00:05:02.868
-I'm just bougie.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:02.868 --> 00:05:05.968
-I mean, basically -- what did
you think happened in the film?

00:05:05.968 --> 00:05:08.801
-I know Spider-Man was, like,
mad about something,

00:05:08.801 --> 00:05:10.167
and then there's a box,
and then there's this man

00:05:10.167 --> 00:05:12.834
who lives in snow.
And I was like, "Who are you?

00:05:12.834 --> 00:05:15.701
Why is there snow in your house?
You look rich.

00:05:15.701 --> 00:05:17.934
Get a -- Can someone just
shovel that [bleep] out?"

00:05:17.934 --> 00:05:20.400
Like --
[ Laughter ]

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:22.901
It was so confusing.
[ Applause ]

00:05:22.901 --> 00:05:25.234
-Yeah, yeah.
That was interesting.

00:05:25.234 --> 00:05:27.634
-I was like, "What a choice."
Like, I just -- I don't know.

00:05:27.634 --> 00:05:28.968
-"What a choice."
-Then there's the Avengers.

00:05:28.968 --> 00:05:30.267
It's like, "What?
They all get together,

00:05:30.267 --> 00:05:32.534
have a slumber party?"
Like, what is the Avengers,

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:33.901
and why do they
all have to get together?

00:05:33.901 --> 00:05:35.133
They all have
their individual movies."

00:05:35.133 --> 00:05:37.767
I don't understand Marvel.
[ Laughter ]

00:05:37.767 --> 00:05:39.267
-You've been doing comedy
for a long time.

00:05:39.267 --> 00:05:40.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:43.968
You're pretty good at it.
But I just heard that you

00:05:43.968 --> 00:05:45.734
auditioned for
"Saturday Night Live"

00:05:45.734 --> 00:05:47.033
at one point.
-I did.

00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:48.100
-I don't remember that.

00:05:48.100 --> 00:05:49.400
What did you do
for your audition?

00:05:49.400 --> 00:05:50.601
Do you remember?
-This was years and years

00:05:50.601 --> 00:05:51.901
and years ago.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:54.467
I do an Oprah impression,
or did an Oprah impression.

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:55.501
And I was trying
to figure out

00:05:55.501 --> 00:05:57.300
what Oprah
would be talking about.

00:05:57.300 --> 00:05:59.000
And I found out there's over,
like, 100 different types

00:05:59.000 --> 00:06:00.968
of lemurs, so it's just --

00:06:00.968 --> 00:06:03.000
The impression is just me
screaming lemur names

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:06.334
in Oprah's voice.
[ Both laugh ]

00:06:06.334 --> 00:06:08.100
No wonder they didn't hire me.

00:06:08.100 --> 00:06:09.267
[ Laughter ]
-I like that.

00:06:09.267 --> 00:06:11.934
-They're like, "What is this?"
-"A lemur!"

00:06:11.934 --> 00:06:14.601
-"A red lemur!"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:14.601 --> 00:06:17.100
-I would watch
the Oprah lemur show.

00:06:17.100 --> 00:06:19.067
-So then I did
a Jamaican Nanny bit,

00:06:19.067 --> 00:06:21.734
and it's based on this real
thing that happened to me.

00:06:21.734 --> 00:06:23.868
I, like, was a nanny,
went to the park,

00:06:23.868 --> 00:06:25.133
and I was like, "'Owdy, ma'am,"

00:06:25.133 --> 00:06:26.300
and this lady looked at me,
and she said,

00:06:26.300 --> 00:06:27.367
"What are you aiming at?"

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.133
'cause she knew
I was faking the accent.

00:06:29.133 --> 00:06:31.767
And I was like,
"Um, I don't know. Friendship?"

00:06:31.767 --> 00:06:33.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:33.868 --> 00:06:36.100
-"You're not supposed
to talk back to me, I'm just --"

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:37.501
-I was, like,
just gonna talk to her.

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:38.667
-Yeah.
-But then she was like,

00:06:38.667 --> 00:06:40.033
"You're a liar."
And I was like, "Oh, okay.

00:06:40.033 --> 00:06:41.501
We go to a different park,"
and I scooped him up,

00:06:41.501 --> 00:06:42.901
and I was like, "We gotta go."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.667
-"We got to get out of here."
Is there anything else

00:06:45.667 --> 00:06:48.234
you want to try that you're
doing all of this stuff?

00:06:48.234 --> 00:06:50.501
-Anything else I want to try?
-I mean, not here on our show,

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:51.734
but I mean in life.
I mean, you're doing --

00:06:51.734 --> 00:06:53.033
-I was like,
"What are we gonna do?"

00:06:53.033 --> 00:06:55.934
-No.
"Bring out the red lemur!"

00:06:55.934 --> 00:06:58.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:58.000 --> 00:07:01.267
But you've done podcasts,
shows --

00:07:01.267 --> 00:07:04.000
I mean, how about a --
-Put me in a movie.

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:07.234
Put me in "Black Panther 2."
"I'm from Wakanda."

00:07:07.234 --> 00:07:09.434
[ Laughs ]
That was a bad accent.

00:07:09.434 --> 00:07:10.634
-No, that was good!

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:11.834
It's not that I want you
to do anything else.

00:07:11.834 --> 00:07:13.467
You're great on "Grand Crew,"
by the way.

00:07:13.467 --> 00:07:15.467
-Thank you.
-And it's a hit show for NBC,

00:07:15.467 --> 00:07:16.934
which we love.

00:07:16.934 --> 00:07:20.200
But can you set up what
"Grand Crew" is about?

00:07:20.200 --> 00:07:22.267
-Sure.
So, it's a bunch of friends

00:07:22.267 --> 00:07:24.300
who hang out in a wine bar,
and they're navigating

00:07:24.300 --> 00:07:26.133
their late 20s, early 30s.

00:07:26.133 --> 00:07:27.434
I don't know if we have ages,

00:07:27.434 --> 00:07:28.667
but, like,
we're having a good time.

00:07:28.667 --> 00:07:29.868
We drink wine.
Wine's fun.

00:07:29.868 --> 00:07:31.634
Gets you drunk.
-That's all they talk about.

00:07:31.634 --> 00:07:33.834
That's what I love.
This was --

00:07:33.834 --> 00:07:34.968
When they developed this,

00:07:34.968 --> 00:07:36.634
they had you in mind
for their character.

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.434
-Yeah, my friend
Phil Augusta Jackson,

00:07:38.434 --> 00:07:40.234
I've known him for
like over a decade.

00:07:40.234 --> 00:07:42.334
We performed here in New York
at the Upright Citizens Brigade

00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:44.367
Theatre, and he was
developing the show.

00:07:44.367 --> 00:07:45.934
And he was like,
"I have a part called 'Nicky.'

00:07:45.934 --> 00:07:47.834
It's based on you.
Would you like to do it?"

00:07:47.834 --> 00:07:49.334
My government name's Nicole,
and I was like,

00:07:49.334 --> 00:07:50.834
"Yeah, it's close.
Let's do this."

00:07:50.834 --> 00:07:53.901
And it got picked up.
And I was, like, you know,

00:07:53.901 --> 00:07:55.534
fortunate enough to be able
to play the part.

00:07:55.534 --> 00:07:57.100
-And did you know the cast
before you started

00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:58.767
working with them?
-Yeah, Echo Kellum and I,

00:07:58.767 --> 00:08:00.834
who plays my brother,
we did sketch together.

00:08:00.834 --> 00:08:02.067
It used to be in L.A.

00:08:02.067 --> 00:08:04.367
Carl Tart,
we do improv together in L.A.

00:08:04.367 --> 00:08:05.934
Aaron Jennings,
we have worked together.

00:08:05.934 --> 00:08:08.868
Grasie Mercedes
and Justin Cunningham,

00:08:08.868 --> 00:08:10.133
we hadn't worked together,
but they, like,

00:08:10.133 --> 00:08:12.167
fit in so wonderfully.
Honestly, like,

00:08:12.167 --> 00:08:15.100
we have so much [bleep] fun.
Like, it's so fun.

00:08:15.100 --> 00:08:16.400
It's not a real job.
-It's a good --

00:08:16.400 --> 00:08:17.801
It's a good vibe.
-Oh, I love it.

00:08:17.801 --> 00:08:18.934
-It's not a real job.

00:08:18.934 --> 00:08:20.367
-Like, we're always just
laughing.

00:08:20.367 --> 00:08:22.100
It doesn't feel like a real job.
-That's what we want to watch.

00:08:22.100 --> 00:08:23.501
That's why people love it,
because you want

00:08:23.501 --> 00:08:24.868
to watch and laugh.

00:08:24.868 --> 00:08:26.901
I want to show everyone a clip.
Here is Nicole Byer

00:08:26.901 --> 00:08:29.133
in "Grand Crew."
Take a look at this.

00:08:29.133 --> 00:08:35.100
♪♪

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:37.601
-Nicky?
Why are you in my home?

00:08:37.601 --> 00:08:41.701
And why are you here
so early in the mo--

00:08:41.701 --> 00:08:44.868
No, no, no, you didn't.

00:08:44.868 --> 00:08:46.701
Standing still
doesn't make you invisible.

00:08:46.701 --> 00:08:48.701
Did you sleep with my brother?
And don't you lie to me.

00:08:48.701 --> 00:08:52.467
-Oh! Yes.
Like, three times last night.

00:08:52.467 --> 00:08:53.734
-Didn't need to know
how many rounds you went.

00:08:53.734 --> 00:08:56.667
Just wanted a yes or no.
-You said don't lie to you.

00:08:56.667 --> 00:08:59.334
Also, two more times
this morning. Ooh!

00:08:59.334 --> 00:09:00.701
[ Laughter ]
-Oh.

00:09:00.701 --> 00:09:02.701
Just because you're
standing still doesn't mean --

00:09:02.701 --> 00:09:04.334
-Ooh!
-Nicole Byer!

00:09:04.334 --> 00:09:08.767
"Grand Crew" airs Tuesday nights
at 8:30 on NBC!

00:09:08.767 --> 00:09:10.300
Fantastic.
Come back, please.

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.801
-Thank you so much
for having me.

